## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates a candidate's ability to design safe, scalable chaos experiments for multi-region, real-time systems with precise blast radius control and explicit recovery criteria. Strong answers demonstrate experience with distributed systems resilience patterns and operational maturity.

## Key Concepts

- Chaos experiments with blast radius and safety constraints
- Multi-region latency, replication lag, and data integrity
- Circuit breakers, backpressure, and local message buffering
- Canary deployments with automated rollback criteria
- Telemetry: RED metrics (Rate, Errors, Duration), p95 latency thresholds, error budgets, and distributed tracing

## Code Example

```javascript
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold, timeout) {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  recordFailure() {
    this.failures++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failures >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
      setTimeout(() => this.state = 'HALF-OPEN', this.timeout);
    }
  }

  recordSuccess() {
    this.failures = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  canExecute() {
    return this.state !== 'OPEN';
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to handle external dependency fragility, multi-tenant isolation, and production risk management. The question evaluates end-to-end instrumentation, resilience patterns, and practical operational procedures rather than theoretical knowledge.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end observability with OpenTelemetry
- Retry budgets with exponential backoff and jitter
- Circuit breakers with configurable thresholds and recovery
- Backpressure through token bucket rate limiting
- Idempotent retries with deduplication keys
- Progressive canary rollouts with automated rollback
- Incident runbooks and alerting thresholds
- SLO/SLI definition and percentile-based monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Circuit breaker around identity provider
class CircuitBreaker {
  constructor(threshold = 5, timeout = 3000) {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.threshold = threshold;
    this.timeout = timeout;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
    this.lastFailure = null;
  }

  async execute(operation) {
    if (this.state === 'OPEN') {
      if (Date.now() - this.lastFailure > this.timeout) {
        this.state = 'HALF_OPEN';
      } else {
        throw new Error('Circuit breaker is OPEN');
      }
    }

    try {
      const result = await operation();
      this.onSuccess();
      return result;
    } catch (error) {
      this.onFailure();
      throw error;
    }
  }

  onSuccess() {
    this.failureCount = 0;
    this.state = 'CLOSED';
  }

  onFailure() {
    this.failureCount++;
    this.lastFailure = Date.now();
    if (this.failureCount >= this.threshold) {
      this.state = 'OPEN';
    }
  }
}
```
